;; ===========================================================================
;; ETCA calling convention mask tests
;;
;; Verifies that getCallPreservedMask() correctly selects CSR masks for
;; different calling conventions (Cold, PreserveMost, PreserveAll).
;;
;; Key invariant demonstrated by test:
;;   Calling a coldcc/preserve_mostcc function from a normal caller
;;   preserves more registers (R1, R2, R7 survive the call), so the
;;   caller does NOT need to spill them.  Calling a default-cc function
;;   requires the caller to save R1, R2 in callee-saved regs (R3/R4).
;;
;; On 16-bit (GN): normal_func saves R3,R4; call_cold does not (✓).
;; On 64-bit (QW/P64): extra GPRs available reduce spills in all cases,
;;   but the mask selection is still exercised and verified.
;; With REX extension: R13-R15 are callee-saved in addition to R3-R4.
;; ===========================================================================

declare i16 @ext_callee(i16)

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Test 1: Default CC — caller must save R1, R2 (caller-saved) before call
;;
;; The function has values in R1 and R2 (arguments v1, v2) needed after the
;; call.  Default CC does NOT preserve R1/R2, so they're moved to callee-saved
;; regs (R3, R4) before the call.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
define i16 @normal_func(i16 %v0, i16 %v1, i16 %v2) {
